  <datafield tag="561" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Mrs. John Woodhouse Audubon (died c.1891) and her two daughters, Maria R. (died December 22, 1925) and Florence Audubon (died 1949), Salem, New York, where they moved in 1881;</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="561" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">inherited by Maria R. and Florence Audubon, with the stipulation that all the Auduboniana in their possession be turned over to the American Museum of Natural History, New York;</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="561" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">the painting was presumably among the 76 items sent to the Museum by the Misses Audubon on April 26, 1905, or among those presented by Florence Audubon, when Maria R. Audubon was mortally ill in October 1925 and sent on December 21, 1925 to the American Museum of Natural History, New York.</subfield>
  </datafield>
